---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="Transparency statement, headquarters, privacy policy, self-funded R&D.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="lead">Transparency statement, headquarters, funding model, privacy.</p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Transparency statement</h2>
      <p>
        We publish what we build, including the failures. The 150-site probe
        results include the blocked sites as well as the working ones. The
        benchmark data includes the runs that failed, not just the wins. If a
        dataset contains rows we could not verify, those rows are flagged
        UNVERIFIED rather than deleted. We do not sell products we have not
        tested, and we do not promise scrapes we have not probed.
      </p>

      <h2>Headquarters</h2>
      <p>
        Stockholm, Sweden. Fully remote, fully distributed: one human (Karl)
        and one autonomous agent (agent1) running the research, engineering,
        and operations. No office, no investors, no ads.
      </p>

      <h2>Funding model: for-profit, self-funded R&amp;D</h2>
      <p>
        Revenue comes from what we sell: data products, custom automation
        scripts, and security audits. That revenue funds the research and
        development. We are deliberately for-profit because profit is the
        constraint that keeps us honest and sustainable. We are deliberately
        self-funded because we answer to the work, not to a term sheet.
      </p>
      <p>
        Costs are small by design: ~$50/month of API spend, a $5/year domain,
        free static hosting. Every major decision is logged in a public-ish
        ledger (governance docs in the repos) with the human as final
        authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy policy (summary)</h2>
      <p>
        This site collects no personal data. We use Cloudflare Web Analytics,
        which is cookieless and privacy-preserving: it reports aggregate page
        views and broad regions, and it never identifies individual visitors.
        No login, no accounts, no newsletter, no tracking pixels from third
        parties.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/privacy">Read the full privacy policy →</a></p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:lillerik.sund@gmail.com">lillerik.sund@gmail.com</a>
        <br />
        <span class="muted">We reply to everything relevant. External actions always wait for human approval.</span>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>